Patchsu patch 9 (optional): remove 'No Fail' from PP calculation.

Needs 0001 + 0002. Also applies together with every other patch (in glob order).

Settings → Patchsu → "Patch 9. Ignore No Fail" → "Remove 'No Fail' from PP calculation" (off by default). While it is on, plays
with No Fail give PP as if No Fail wasn't selected: the NF PP reduction (osu! up to -10% by misses, catch -10%,
mania -25%) is gone. The play itself keeps NF (mods, score multiplier, leaderboards show it as before).

"Also remove 'No Fail' score reduction" (off by default, only while the option above is on): NF plays show their
total score without NF's x0.5 multiplier (x2) everywhere scores are shown (leaderboards, results, HUD, profile
ranked / total score), and leaderboards, the results screen's score panels and the in-game leaderboard sort by that score. The stored score is never changed.

  Applies to:   every PP calculation — results screen, leaderboard PP and tooltip, the in-game PP counter,
                0003's PP sort, 0006's simulation, local profile PP / best scores / other profiles' chips.
  Toggling:     the profile page recalculates, the song select leaderboard is fetched again, and the active
                profile's PP / estimated rank change shows on the toolbar (like the other PP options in 0002).

How it works (for later patches):
- osu.Game/LocalPriority/LocalNoFailPerformance.cs: the settings (the "NoFail" section of PatchsuSettings.json from 0001;
  an old patchsu-osu/patch12.json is taken over once and deleted) and Apply(score), which gives the calculator a clone of the score
  without NF. An AsyncLocal override (RunWith / Pin) lets one calculation use the other setting (for the toolbar's
  before/after) and keeps a profile calculation on one setting even if it changes midway.
- PerformanceCalculator.CalculateAsync / Calculate (base class, osu.Game) call Apply: one hook for all rulesets,
  away from 0500's hunk in OsuPerformanceCalculator.
- Profile PP: 0002's performance-cache.json keeps the normal values; NF plays calculated without NF are cached in
  patchsu-osu/performance-cache-without-nofail.json, so toggling never recalculates every play.
- LocalProfileManager.NoFail.cs: SetIgnoreNoFailPerformance (save, revision++, leaderboard refresh, toolbar
  before/after). LocalNoFailPerformanceSettings.cs: the "Patch 9. Ignore No Fail" subsection (a
  PatchSettingsSubsection from 0001, found and sorted by patch number, so LocalPrioritySection isn't edited).
- Small hunks in 0002 files: LocalProfileStore (Load after BeatmapTags),
  LocalProfileStatistics (ScoreSummary.HasNoFail, the NF branch at the top of the PP cache loop, ScoreSummary.TotalScore as shown).
- Score display: Scoring/Legacy/ScoreInfoExtensions.GetDisplayScore (both overloads) and Scoring/ScoreInfoExtensions
  (OrderByTotalScore, the Score sort) use LocalNoFailPerformance.DisplayTotalScore. The ScoreInfoExtensions section is
  written with one line of context so it applies with or without 0003's hunk next to it.
  Ranking/ScorePanelList (panel order), Ranking/SoloResultsScreen (own better score check) and
  Play/Leaderboards/SoloGameplayLeaderboardProvider (HUD order, only while the score option is on) compare the score as shown.
- Saved PP: ScoreInfo.PP was saved with No Fail, so Ranking/Expanded/Statistics/PerformanceStatistic (results screen) and
  Select/BeatmapLeaderboardScore.Tooltip (leaderboard PP) skip it for No Fail plays while No Fail is ignored
  (LocalNoFailPerformance.IgnoresSavedPerformance) and calculate instead. Written without leading context so they apply with or without 0004.

diff --git a/osu.Game/LocalPriority/LocalNoFailPerformance.cs b/osu.Game/LocalPriority/LocalNoFailPerformance.cs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..2df51140e9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/osu.Game/LocalPriority/LocalNoFailPerformance.cs
@@ -0,0 +1,298 @@
+// Patched for fun and personal needs. I suggest playing osu!lazer instead of this client. All modifications are done with AI from personal interest.
+// Peppy openly stated that he does not like using AI and we completely respect it. I only do it for research purposes and to see what features I would love in lazer.
+// To use it you'll need to compile it on your PC using provided .sh / .cmd files.
+// This client modification does not break any osu! rules or terms of service and do not conflict with osu! rules for account banning
+// However, I do not take any liablity if your account will be banned for accessing beatmap, leaderboard and metadata downloading
+// Use responsibly and preferably local-only.
+
+using System;
+using System.Collections.Generic;
+using System.IO;
+using System.Linq;
+using System.Threading;
+using System.Threading.Tasks;
+using Newtonsoft.Json;
+using osu.Framework.Bindables;
+using osu.Framework.Logging;
+using osu.Framework.Platform;
+using osu.Game.Rulesets.Mods;
+using osu.Game.Scoring;
+
+namespace osu.Game.LocalPriority
+{
+    /// <summary>
+    /// Patch 9: Settings → Patchsu → "Patch 9. Ignore No Fail" → "Remove 'No Fail' from PP calculation".
+    /// While it is on, every PP calculation (results screen, leaderboards, the HUD counter, profiles) treats plays as if
+    /// No Fail wasn't selected, so its PP reduction is gone. The play itself (its mods and score) is never changed.
+    /// With "Also remove 'No Fail' score reduction" on as well, No Fail plays show (and sort by) their total score as if No Fail wasn't selected.
+    /// The settings are kept in the "NoFail" section of PatchsuSettings.json (they used to be in "osu-local/patch12.json",
+    /// which is taken over once and deleted).
+    /// </summary>
+    public static class LocalNoFailPerformance
+    {
+        private const string settings_section = @"NoFail";
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Where the settings were kept before PatchsuSettings.json.
+        /// </summary>
+        private const string old_settings_file = LocalProfileStore.DIRECTORY + @"/patch12.json";
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// PP of No Fail plays calculated without No Fail. The profile PP cache keeps the normal values, so turning this on or off
+        /// never recalculates every play.
+        /// </summary>
+        private const string performance_file = LocalProfileStore.DIRECTORY + @"/performance-cache-without-nofail.json";
+
+        private static readonly object sync = new object();
+        private static readonly AsyncLocal<bool?> override_value = new AsyncLocal<bool?>();
+
+        private static Storage? storage;
+        private static Bindable<bool>? enabledSetting;
+        private static Bindable<bool>? scoreEnabledSetting;
+        private static Dictionary<Guid, double?> performanceCache = new Dictionary<Guid, double?>();
+        private static bool savePending;
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// The saved setting.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static bool Enabled { get; private set; }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// The saved "Also remove 'No Fail' score reduction" setting (only used while <see cref="Enabled"/> is on).
+        /// </summary>
+        public static bool ScoreEnabled { get; private set; }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Whether total scores of No Fail plays are shown without No Fail's score multiplier.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static bool IgnoreScore => Enabled && ScoreEnabled;
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// No Fail's score multiplier, the same in every ruleset (it is never part of a mod combination's multiplier).
+        /// </summary>
+        public const double SCORE_MULTIPLIER = 0.5;
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Whether a PP calculation running now ignores No Fail: the setting, unless this calculation was told otherwise
+        /// (to compare PP with and without it).
+        /// </summary>
+        public static bool Ignore => override_value.Value ?? Enabled;
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Called once the local profile store is created.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static void Load(Storage gameStorage)
+        {
+            lock (sync)
+            {
+                storage = gameStorage;
+                var settings = PatchsuSettings.Current;
+                enabledSetting = settings.GetBindable(settings_section, @"IgnoreNoFail", false);
+                scoreEnabledSetting = settings.GetBindable(settings_section, @"IgnoreNoFailScore", false);
+
+                if (storage.Exists(old_settings_file))
+                {
+                    if (read<SettingsData>(old_settings_file) is SettingsData old)
+                    {
+                        enabledSetting.Value = old.IgnoreNoFail;
+                        scoreEnabledSetting.Value = old.IgnoreNoFailScore;
+                    }
+
+                    try
+                    {
+                        storage.Delete(old_settings_file);
+                    }
+                    catch (Exception e)
+                    {
+                        Logger.Error(e, $@"Patchsu: could not delete {old_settings_file}.");
+                    }
+                }
+
+                Enabled = enabledSetting.Value;
+                ScoreEnabled = scoreEnabledSetting.Value;
+                performanceCache = read<Dictionary<Guid, double?>>(performance_file) ?? new Dictionary<Guid, double?>();
+            }
+        }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Saves the setting. Use <see cref="LocalProfileManager.SetIgnoreNoFailPerformance"/> to also update profiles.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static void SetEnabled(bool enabled)
+        {
+            lock (sync)
+            {
+                Enabled = enabled;
+                (enabledSetting ??= PatchsuSettings.Current.GetBindable(settings_section, @"IgnoreNoFail", false)).Value = enabled;
+            }
+        }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Saves "Also remove 'No Fail' score reduction". Use <see cref="LocalProfileManager.SetIgnoreNoFailScore"/> to also update displays.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static void SetScoreEnabled(bool enabled)
+        {
+            lock (sync)
+            {
+                ScoreEnabled = enabled;
+                (scoreEnabledSetting ??= PatchsuSettings.Current.GetBindable(settings_section, @"IgnoreNoFailScore", false)).Value = enabled;
+            }
+        }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// A total score as shown: without No Fail's reduction when <see cref="IgnoreScore"/> is on and the play used No Fail.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static long DisplayTotalScore(long totalScore, bool hasNoFail)
+            => hasNoFail && IgnoreScore ? (long)Math.Round(totalScore / SCORE_MULTIPLIER) : totalScore;
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// <see cref="DisplayTotalScore(long, bool)"/> of a play, for showing and sorting (its mods are only looked at while the setting is on).
+        /// </summary>
+        public static long DisplayTotalScore(IScoreInfo score)
+            => IgnoreScore ? DisplayTotalScore(score.TotalScore, score.Mods.Any(m => m.Acronym == @"NF")) : score.TotalScore;
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// The score to calculate PP for: without No Fail while it is ignored, otherwise the score itself.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static ScoreInfo Apply(ScoreInfo score)
+        {
+            // Acronyms first: building the score's mods makes new mod instances, which most plays (no No Fail) never need.
+            if (!Ignore || !HasNoFail(score))
+                return score;
+
+            var mods = score.Mods;
+
+            if (!mods.Any(m => m is ModNoFail))
+                return score;
+
+            var clone = score.DeepClone();
+            clone.Mods = mods.Where(m => m is not ModNoFail).ToArray();
+            return clone;
+        }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Runs a calculation with No Fail ignored or not, whatever the setting is.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static async Task<T> RunWith<T>(bool ignore, Func<Task<T>> calculation)
+        {
+            override_value.Value = ignore;
+            return await calculation().ConfigureAwait(false);
+        }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// For a calculation of many plays (call it from an async method): keeps the current setting until that method returns,
+        /// so changing the setting midway doesn't mix both kinds of PP.
+        /// </summary>
+        /// <returns>Whether No Fail is ignored.</returns>
+        public static bool Pin()
+        {
+            bool ignore = Ignore;
+            override_value.Value = ignore;
+            return ignore;
+        }
+
+        public static bool HasNoFail(ScoreInfo score) => score.APIMods.Any(m => m.Acronym == @"NF");
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Whether a play's saved PP can't be shown (results screen, leaderboard tooltip): it was saved with No Fail,
+        /// so a No Fail play is calculated again while No Fail is ignored.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static bool IgnoresSavedPerformance(ScoreInfo score) => Ignore && HasNoFail(score);
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// The PP of a No Fail play without No Fail, from the cache or calculated once.
+        /// </summary>
+        /// <param name="scoreId">The play.</param>
+        /// <param name="loadScore">Loads the play when it needs calculating.</param>
+        /// <param name="calculate">Calculates the PP (No Fail must be ignored when this runs): the PP, and whether the beatmap failed to calculate.</param>
+        public static async Task<double?> GetPerformanceAsync(Guid scoreId, Func<ScoreInfo?> loadScore, Func<ScoreInfo, Task<(double? PP, bool Failed)>> calculate)
+        {
+            lock (sync)
+            {
+                if (performanceCache.TryGetValue(scoreId, out double? cached))
+                    return cached;
+            }
+
+            var score = loadScore();
+
+            if (score == null)
+                return null;
+
+            var (pp, failed) = await calculate(score).ConfigureAwait(false);
+
+            // Same as the profile PP cache: plays on missing beatmaps are tried again later, beatmaps that fail are remembered.
+            if (pp != null || failed)
+            {
+                lock (sync)
+                {
+                    performanceCache[scoreId] = pp;
+                    saveCache();
+                }
+            }
+
+            return pp;
+        }
+
+        private static void saveCache()
+        {
+            if (savePending)
+                return;
+
+            savePending = true;
+
+            Task.Delay(500).ContinueWith(_ =>
+            {
+                lock (sync)
+                {
+                    savePending = false;
+                    write(performance_file, performanceCache);
+                }
+            });
+        }
+
+        private static T? read<T>(string filename)
+            where T : class
+        {
+            try
+            {
+                if (storage == null || !storage.Exists(filename))
+                    return null;
+
+                using (var stream = storage.GetStream(filename, FileAccess.Read, FileMode.Open))
+                using (var reader = new StreamReader(stream))
+                    return JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<T>(reader.ReadToEnd());
+            }
+            catch (Exception e)
+            {
+                Logger.Error(e, $@"Patchsu: could not read {filename}.");
+                return null;
+            }
+        }
+
+        private static void write(string filename, object value)
+        {
+            if (storage == null)
+                return;
+
+            try
+            {
+                using (var stream = storage.CreateFileSafely(filename))
+                using (var writer = new StreamWriter(stream))
+                using (var json = new JsonTextWriter(writer))
+                    JsonSerializer.CreateDefault(new JsonSerializerSettings { Formatting = Formatting.Indented }).Serialize(json, value);
+            }
+            catch (Exception e)
+            {
+                Logger.Error(e, $@"Patchsu: could not save {filename}.");
+            }
+        }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// The old patch12.json.
+        /// </summary>
+        private class SettingsData
+        {
+            public bool IgnoreNoFail { get; set; }
+            public bool IgnoreNoFailScore { get; set; }
+        }
+    }
+}
